  "visualLines": [
    {
      "lineId": 0,
      "y": 746.58,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "NIST SP 800-207 ZERO TRUST ARCHITECTURE",
      "itemIndexes": [
        0,
        1,
        2
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 1,
      "y": 706.62,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "• Enterprise public key infrastructure (PKI): This system is responsible for generating",
      "itemIndexes": [
        8,
        9,
        10,
        11,
        12
      ],
      "firstX": 90
    },
    {
      "lineId": 2,
      "y": 692.82,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "and logging certificates issued by the enterprise to resources, subjects, services and",
      "itemIndexes": [
        13
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 3,
      "y": 679.02,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "applications. This also includes the global certificate authority ecosystem and the Federal",
      "itemIndexes": [
        14
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 4,
      "y": 667.47,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "PKI, 4 which may or may not be integrated with the enterprise PKI. This could also be a",
      "itemIndexes": [
        15,
        16,
        17,
        18
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 5,
      "y": 651.42,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "PKI that is not built upon X.509 certificates.",
      "itemIndexes": [
        19
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 6,
      "y": 630.78,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "• ID management system: This is responsible for creating, storing, and managing",
      "itemIndexes": [
        21,
        22,
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "firstX": 90
    },
    {
      "lineId": 7,
      "y": 616.98,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "enterprise user accounts and identity records (e.g., lightweight directory access protocol",
      "itemIndexes": [
        26
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 8,
      "y": 603.18,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "(LDAP) server). This system contains the necessary subject information (e.g., name,",
      "itemIndexes": [
        27
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 9,
      "y": 589.38,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "email address, certificates) and other enterprise characteristics such as role, access",
      "itemIndexes": [
        28
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 10,
      "y": 575.58,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "attributes, and assigned assets. This system often utilizes other systems (such as a PKI)",
      "itemIndexes": [
        29
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 11,
      "y": 560.52,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "This publication is available free of charge from: https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-207 for artifacts associated with user accounts. This system may be part of a larger federated",
      "itemIndexes": [
        6,
        30
      ],
      "firstX": 19.68
    },
    {
      "lineId": 12,
      "y": 547.98,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "community and may include nonenterprise employees or links to nonenterprise assets for",
      "itemIndexes": [
        31
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 13,
      "y": 534.18,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "collaboration.",
      "itemIndexes": [
        32
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 14,
      "y": 513.54,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "• Security information and event management (SIEM) system: This collects security-",
      "itemIndexes": [
        34,
        35,
        36,
        37,
        38
      ],
      "firstX": 90
    },
    {
      "lineId": 15,
      "y": 499.74,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "centric information for later analysis. This data is then used to refine policies and warn of",
      "itemIndexes": [
        39
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 16,
      "y": 485.94,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "possible attacks against enterprise assets.",
      "itemIndexes": [
        40
      ],
      "firstX": 108
    },
    {
      "lineId": 17,
      "y": 461.04,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "3.1 Variations of Zero Trust Architecture Approaches",
      "itemIndexes": [
        42,
        43,
        44
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 18,
      "y": 435.48,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "There are several ways that an enterprise can enact a ZTA for workflows. These approaches vary",
      "itemIndexes": [
        46
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 19,
      "y": 421.68,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "in the components used and in the main source of policy rules for an organization. Each",
      "itemIndexes": [
        47
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 20,
      "y": 407.88,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "approach implements all the tenets of ZT (see Section 2.1 ) but may use one or two (or one",
      "itemIndexes": [
        48,
        49,
        50,
        51
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 21,
      "y": 394.08,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "component) as the main driver of policies. A full ZT solution will include elements of all three",
      "itemIndexes": [
        52
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 22,
      "y": 380.28,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "approaches. The approaches include enhanced identity governance–driven, logical micro-",
      "itemIndexes": [
        53
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 23,
      "y": 366.48,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "segmentation, and network-based segmentation.",
      "itemIndexes": [
        54
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 24,
      "y": 340.68,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "Certain approaches lend themselves to some use cases more than others. An organization looking",
      "itemIndexes": [
        56
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 25,
      "y": 326.88,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "to develop a ZTA for its enterprise may find that its chosen use case and existing policies point",
      "itemIndexes": [
        57
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 26,
      "y": 313.08,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "to one approach over others. That does not mean the other approaches would not work but rather",
      "itemIndexes": [
        58
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 27,
      "y": 299.28,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "that other approaches may be more difficult to implement and may require more fundamental",
      "itemIndexes": [
        59
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 28,
      "y": 285.48,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "changes to how the enterprise currently conducts business flows.",
      "itemIndexes": [
        60
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 29,
      "y": 260.58,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "3.1.1 ZTA Using Enhanced Identity Governance",
      "itemIndexes": [
        62,
        63,
        64
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 30,
      "y": 235.02,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "The enhanced identity governance approach to developing a ZTA uses the identity of actors as",
      "itemIndexes": [
        66
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 31,
      "y": 221.22,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "the key component of policy creation. If it were not for subjects requesting access to enterprise",
      "itemIndexes": [
        67
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 32,
      "y": 207.42,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "resources, there would be no need to create access polices. For this approach, enterprise resource",
      "itemIndexes": [
        68
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 33,
      "y": 193.62,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "access policies are based on identity and assigned attributes. The primary requirement for",
      "itemIndexes": [
        69
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 34,
      "y": 179.82,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "resource access is based on the access privileges granted to the given subject. Other factors such",
      "itemIndexes": [
        70
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 35,
      "y": 166.02,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "as device used, asset status, and environmental factors may alter the final confidence level",
      "itemIndexes": [
        71
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 36,
      "y": 152.22,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "calculation (and ultimate access authorization) or tailor the result in some way, such as granting",
      "itemIndexes": [
        72
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 37,
      "y": 138.42,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "only partial access to a given data source based on network location. Individual resources or PEP",
      "itemIndexes": [
        73
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
      "lineId": 38,
      "y": 98.3,
      "height": 12,
      "text": "4 https://www.idmanagement.gov/topics/fpki/",
      "itemIndexes": [
        75,
        76,
        77
      ],
      "firstX": 72
    },
    {
